      "description": "Seria® was released in 2000. It can be seen as a 'literary' typeface, with long ascenders and descenders and a distinctive upright italic. Its relatively small x-height makes Seria a rewarding challenge for the experienced typographer.\n\nAugmenting Seria with a sans serif version was an obvious next step. Using a black marker and some white paint, the serifed characters were transformed into a sans, resulting in Seria Sans, which retains the same long ascenders and descenders as Seria, quite unusual for a sans serif.\n\nIn 2003, the Seria family won two awards: a Certificate of Excellence from the ISTD and a Certificate of Excellence in Type Design from ATypI.",
